>> title: Chicken Cacciatore
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, tomatoes, mushrooms, italian, one-pot, skillet
>> counters: One Pot
>> aka: hunter's chicken, pollo alla cacciatora, chicken chasseur, chicken hunter style
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: Everything after the browning happens in the fat and the fond it left, so the pan is never wiped or changed.
>> step.2: brown 10 min, skin side down
>> step.3: soften 8 min in the fat
>> step.4: deglaze, 2 min
>> step.5: braise covered 35 min
>> step.6: reduce uncovered 8 min
>> step.7: Brown it well, accept the skin goes soft under the lid, and drive the sauce down uncovered for eight minutes.

Hunter's chicken, which means what was to hand: a bird, mushrooms, whatever peppers were on the sill, and one pan carried out to cook it in. Everything after the browning happens in the fat and the fond the browning left, so the pan is never wiped and never changed.

Brown @bone-in chicken thighs{3%lb}(1.4 kg; skin on, patted dry), @kosher salt{2%tsp} in @olive oil{2%Tbs} in a #large skillet{} for ~brown{10%min}.

Soften @&(~1)browned chicken{} with @cremini mushrooms{8%oz}(225 g; quartered), @red bell pepper{1%large}(sliced), @yellow onion{1%medium}(sliced), @garlic{4%cloves}(sliced) for ~saute{8%min}.

Deglaze @&(~1)pan{} with @dry white wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL) for ~simmer{2%min}, scraping the bottom clean.

Braise @&(~1)pan{} covered with @canned whole tomatoes{28%oz}(800 g; crushed by hand), @rosemary{1%sprig}, @bay leaf{1} for ~braise{35%min}.

Reduce @&(~1)cacciatore{} uncovered with @black olives{1/2%cup}(85 g; pitted), @flat-leaf parsley{1/4%cup}(chopped) for ~simmer{8%min}.

The skin will not stay crisp under a lid and chasing that is how people end up with two pans. Brown it well, accept that it goes soft, and spend the last eight minutes uncovered driving the sauce down onto the chicken instead.
